{
  "title": "Madrid, Spain",
  "indexDescription": "A family trip to Madrid in 2009.",
  "description": "We visited Madrid at the end of 2009 as part of our three-week family trip to Spain over Christmas.\n\nWe stayed in the heart of the city and walked everywhere.\n\nWe had a nice dinner at a restaurant across the street.  The waiter was very nice and gave us, kids included, free after-dinner limoncello as a New Year celebration.\n\nWe visited the three big museums of Madrid: Museo Nacional del Prado, Museo Nacional Centro de Arte Reina Sofía, and Museo Nacional Thyssen-Bornemisza.\n\nWe might have gone into CaixaForum, I'm not sure, but I have pictures of it and the plant wall.\n\nKathleen remembers Alex saying, \"I haven't seen a painting called Bathers that I didn't like.\"",
